{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P20382","secondaryAccessions":["Q16044","Q8WVG0"],"uniProtkbId":"MCH_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1991-02-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2009-05-05","entryVersion":191,"sequenceVersion":3},"annotationScore":5,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Pro-MCH"}},"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Neuropeptide-glycine-glutamic acid"},"shortNames":[{"value":"NGE"},{"value":"Neuropeptide G-E"}]}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P56942"}],"value":"Neuropeptide-glutamic acid-isoleucine"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P56942"}],"value":"NEI"},{"value":"Neuropeptide E-I"}]}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"38710677"}],"value":"Melanin-concentrating hormone"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"38710677"}],"value":"MCH"}]}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:9109"}],"value":"PMCH"},"synonyms":[{"value":"MCH"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P14200"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P56942"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15340116"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"38710677"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"39616153"}],"value":"Neuropeptide ligand for the G protein-coupled receptor MCHR1 and MCHR2 that can activate both G(i/o)- and G(q/11)-dependent signaling pathways (PubMed:15340116, PubMed:38710677, PubMed:39616153). Acts as a neuromodulator in the central nervous system, promoting feeding, positive energy balance (orexigenic) and sleep. Inhibits stimulated ACTH release (lowering plasma glucocorticoids), consistent with a role in down-regulating hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis activity. Functionally antagonizes melanotropin alpha (alpha-MSH), opposing its inhibitory effect on food intake and exploratory behaviors and its stimulatory effect on the HPA axis. Antagonizes NEI-induced behavioral effects (By similarity). May also participate in spermatocyte differentiation (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Melanin-concentrating hormone"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P14200"}],"value":"Neuropeptide that modulates stress-related neuroendocrine responses and behaviors. Stimulates ACTH secretion, functionally counteracting the ACTH-suppressing action of MCH; the underlying mechanism is not fully characterized. Reduces dopamine and DOPAC release in the ventromedial nucleus. Influences differentiation of neuronal processes and affects neurofilament protein content in vitro"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Neuropeptide-glutamic acid-isoleucine"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Melanin-concentrating hormone","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"15340116"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"38710677"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"39616153"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Neuropeptide-glutamic acid-isoleucine","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P14200"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9191099"}],"value":"Expressed in lateral hypothalamus"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY","molecule":"Melanin-concentrating hormone"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9191099"}],"value":"Expressed in lateral hypothalamus"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY","molecule":"Neuropeptide-glutamic acid-isoleucine"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9191099"}],"value":"Predominantly expressed in lateral hypothalamus, also detected in pallidum, neocortex and cerebellum. Also found in thymus, brown adipose tissue, duodenum and testis (spermatogonia, early spermatocytes and Sertoli cells). No expression in peripheral blood. In peripheral tissues a large product, encompassing the NEI and MCH domains of the precursor, is found predominantly"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10037747"}],"value":"Differentially processed in the brain and in peripheral organs producing two neuropeptides; NEI and MCH. A third peptide, NGE, may also be produced. Preferential processing in neurons by prohormone convertase 2 (PC2) generates NEI. MCH is generated in neurons of the lateral hypothalmic area by several prohormone convertases including PC1/3, PC2 and PC5/6"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the melanin-concentrating hormone family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":21,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":22,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":165,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Pro-MCH","featureId":"PRO_0000019104"},{"type":"Peptide","location":{"start":{"value":110,"modifier":"EXACT"},"en